= Uniform Resource Identifier — Technical =

RFC 3986 defines generic URI syntax around scheme and hierarchical or scheme-specific components. Interpretation depends on the scheme. Web architecture uses URIs to preserve global identification independently from the current state or representation of the identified resource.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* URI ≠ network location necessarily
* URI ≠ domain name
* identifier ≠ representation

== References ==
* IETF RFC 3986, ''Uniform Resource Identifier (URI): Generic Syntax'' (2005).
* W3C, ''Architecture of the World Wide Web, Volume One'', Recommendation, 15 December 2004.
